  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBQA-F001-AI34" ;
  triage:title "Potential duplicate/dead code in CLI's GraftNudgeSink endpoint resolution vs daemon's canonical implementation" ;
  triage:description "CRITICAL REVIEWER DISAGREEMENT. ruthless-boundary-qa reports: crates/atm/src/commands/internal_nudge.rs:165-196 (GraftNudgeSink::deliver) is a second, independent implementation of graft endpoint resolution that uses home::atm_home() (local process home) instead of canonical_graft_root/roster resolver introduced in this PR. BuiltInNudgeSinkTarget::Graft trigger may be dead code (repo-wide grep found no callers outside internal_nudge.rs's own match arm and test fixtures). Counter-assessment from arch-qa: GraftNudgeSink is intentional, implements a different use case (CLI's own local resolution) vs daemon's roster-based resolution; graft_receiver_record_path_from_home is a thin wrapper for existing call sites, not a duplicated independent implementation. FIND ING RECORDS BOTH POSITIONS without resolution — team-lead/arch-ctm must verify reachability of BuiltInNudgeSinkTarget::Graft in production and decide fix vs no-fix." ;
